# Applies to every image built from this repo root as build context
# (deploy/docker/platform-api.Dockerfile and deploy/docker/
# frontend.Dockerfile both build with `.` as context - see
# deploy/docker/README.md). Keeps the build context small AND makes sure
# nothing gitignored-but-locally-present (a developer's own .env, a local
# node_modules/dist from a native `npm run build`) can ever be COPYed into
# an image layer, even an intermediate/discarded multi-stage one -
# CLAUDE.md's "never store secrets in ... config files checked into git"
# extends to "never let them ride along into a build context" too.
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/node_modules
**/dist
